<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Bonney Butte and Meadows from Bennett Pass</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:189-2: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.310224" lon="-121.641836"><ele>1426.3</ele><name>Bennett Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 367401558 'Bennet Pass Sno-Park'); Forest Road 3550 passes 6 m from it; confidence: high; pdf_page: 188; book_elev_ft: 4674; quote: The trail starts at Bennett Pass Sno-Park and goes 2.4 miles to the Terrible Traverse along a splendid, rolling, forested ridge following a primitive road</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.298990" lon="-121.608880"><ele>1463.9</ele><name>Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse)</name><desc>source: OSM node 5164478227 on Forest Road 3550, the DEM low point (4,803 ft) 2.28 mi along the road; the road then sidehills north of the crest; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 189; book_elev_ft: 4800; quote: the trail descends to Windy Saddle at the west foot of the Terrible Traverse, which is a steep 180-yard-long sidehill traverse on the north side of the ridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.279071" lon="-121.596332"><ele>1632.9</ele><name>Bonney Junction</name><desc>source: OSM node 3669713797 (Gunsight Trailhead), where Forest Road 4891 leaves Forest Road 3550; DEM 5,357 ft; confidence: high; pdf_page: 191; book_elev_ft: 5360; quote: At Bonney Junction (5,360 feet), a forested saddle, roads lead to Camp Windy and Bonney Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.262817" lon="-121.592985"><ele>1707.9</ele><name>Bonney Butte summit</name><desc>source: OSM node 357307332 Bonney Butte (natural=peak); Forest Road 4891-130 ends beside it; confidence: high; pdf_page: 192; book_elev_ft: 5560; quote: turn off to the right and either follow an old road to the south foot of the butte as it circles upward to the crest, or just ski through small, widely set firs to the top</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Bonney Butte and Meadows from Bennett Pass</name><desc>1. Bennett Pass Sno-Park -&gt; Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse): osm (high), 2.24 mi | 2. Windy Saddle (west foot of the Terrible Traverse) -&gt; Bonney Junction: osm (high), 1.78 mi | 3. Bonney Junction -&gt; Bonney Butte summit: osm (medium), 1.51 mi</desc>
